ile once. Do not re-run git or crawl the codebase. Read-only.\n\n## Focus points\n- Is `PgProducerStore` correct? Especially: `upsert` on-conflict semantics; the `touch_last_seen`/`set_revoked` read-modify-write of the JSONB `record` (does reassigning `row.record = new_dict` correctly mark the column dirty so it persists?); `get_by_key_prefix` querying the generated `key_prefix` column.\n- Is modifying `tests/common/msging/test_store.py` acceptable? (It's a msging TEST, not production; the assertion was stale after the postgres backend became real.) Is the new assertion correct?\n- Is the `pytest.ini` `. src` change sound and non-harmful?\n- No msging PRODUCTION code touched?\n\n## Output Format\n### Spec Compliance — ✅ | ❌ (file:line) | ⚠️\n### Strengths\n### Issues — Critical / Important / Minor (file:line, what, why, fix)\n### Assessment — **Task quality:** Approved | Needs fixes; **Reasoning:** 1-2 sentences.\nBegin directly with the verdict.",
